{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G1WRRFMFkVj7EWso1BK865","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# QuantAgent-bdm — Requirements — Fix tests expecting shared state updates across multi-agent calls\n2\t\n3\t## Objective\n4\tAlign the test suite with the intended LangGraph state contract:\n5\t- Analysis agents (Indicator/Pattern/Trend) **return structured reports** and **do not update** shared `messages` state.\n6\t- Only the Decision Agent updates `messages`.\n7\t\n8\t## Context\n9\tThe repository design explicitly separates:\n10\t- **Inter-agent communication** via structured reports (`IndicatorReport`, `PatternReport`, `TrendReport`)\n11\t- **Conversation history** (`messages`) owned/updated by the Decision Agent only\n12\t\n13\tSee: `docs/03_design/MESSAGE_STATE_MANAGEMENT.md`.\n14\t\n15\t## In Scope\n16\t- Update tests that:\n17\t  - call multiple agents (sequentially or via compiled graph) and expect `state[\"messages\"]` to be updated by analysis agents\n18\t  - assert that all agents “produce messages”\n19\t- Tests should instead verify:\n20\t  - analysis agents return their respective structured report keys\n21\t  - `messages` is unchanged/absent until the Decision Agent runs\n22\t  - the compiled graph output includes `messages` **because** the Decision Agent ran\n23\t\n24\t## Out of Scope\n25\t- Changes to production agent behavior/state schema (unless a true mismatch is discovered)\n26\t- Rewriting unrelated tests for style/coverage\n27\t- Changing model/provider behavior\n28\t\n29\t## Constraints\n30\t- Keep changes minimal and localized to failing/incorrect assertions.\n31\t- Do not introduce test patterns that validate mocks instead of behavior (see `docs/03_design/TESTING_PATTERNS.md`).\n32\t\n33\t## Definition of Done\n34\t- Tests no longer assume shared `messages` updates across analysis-agent calls.\n35\t- Tests assert structured report outputs for analysis agents.\n36\t- Final graph invocation tests assert presence of `messages` only at/after Decision Agent.\n37\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c1eaaa5-4630-4080-9c30-fa243b2053bf","uuid":"b4745e99-96e0-45bd-a3f5-d411c00fb790","timestamp":"2026-05-08T02:42:41.266Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/01_requirements/QuantAgent-bdm-RQ-fix-tests-shared-state.md","content":"# QuantAgent-bdm — Requirements — Fix tests expecting shared state updates across multi-agent calls\n\n## Objective\nAlign the test suite with the intended LangGraph state contract:\n- Analysis agents (Indicator/Pattern/Trend) **return structured reports** and **do not update** shared `messages` state.\n- Only the Decision Agent updates `messages`.\n\n## Context\nThe repository design explicitly separates:\n- **Inter-agent communication** via structured reports (`IndicatorReport`, `PatternReport`, `TrendReport`)\n- **Conversation history** (`messages`) owned/updated by the Decision Agent only\n\nSee: `docs/03_design/MESSAGE_STATE_MANAGEMENT.md`.\n\n## In Scope\n- Update tests that:\n  - call multiple agents (sequentially or via compiled graph) and expect `state[\"messages\"]` to be updated by analysis agents\n  - assert that all agents “produce messages”\n- Tests should instead verify:\n  - analysis agents return their respective structured report keys\n  - `messages` is unchanged/absent until the Decision Agent runs\n  - the compiled graph output includes `messages` **because** the Decision Agent ran\n\n## Out of Scope\n- Changes to production agent behavior/state schema (unless a true mismatch is discovered)\n- Rewriting unrelated tests for style/coverage\n- Changing model/provider behavior\n\n## Constraints\n- Keep changes minimal and localized to failing/incorrect assertions.\n- Do not introduce test patterns that validate mocks instead of behavior (see `docs/03_design/TESTING_PATTERNS.md`).\n\n## Definition of Done\n- Tests no longer assume shared `messages` updates across analysis-agent calls.\n- Tests assert structured report outputs for analysis agents.\n- Final graph invocation tests assert presence of `messages` only at/after Decision Agent.\n","numLines":37,"startLine":1,"totalLines":37}}}
