{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KLDJyHXzEk53UPQjwUokEJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# QuantAgent-4ch — Planning: Test Database Configuration\n2\t\n3\t**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-4ch  \n4\t**Title:** Fix remaining unit test failures (stale paths and missing data)  \n5\t**Type:** Bug  \n6\t**Priority:** 1\n7\t\n8\t---\n9\t\n10\t## Objective\n11\t\n12\tFix unit test failures by replacing PostgreSQL database dependency with SQLite for tests.\n13\t\n14\t---\n15\t\n16\t## Tasks\n17\t\n18\t### Task 1: Update conftest.py with db_session Fixture\n19\t**Estimate:** 0.5h\n20\t\n21\t**What:**\n22\t- Add `db_session` fixture to `tests/conftest.py`\n23\t- Use SQLite in-memory engine (`sqlite:///:memory:`)\n24\t- Create all tables via `Base.metadata.create_all()`\n25\t- Yield session for test use\n26\t- Cleanup: close session, drop tables, dispose engine\n27\t\n28\t**Why:**\n29\t- Provides isolated, fast test database\n30\t- No external dependencies (PostgreSQL)\n31\t\n32\t**How to validate:**\n33\t```bash\n34\tpytest tests/test_backtest.py::TestBacktest::test_backtest_initialization -v\n35\t# Should PASS (no psycopg2 errors)\n36\t```\n37\t\n38\t**Dependencies:** None\n39\t\n40\t---\n41\t\n42\t### Task 2: Enable SQLite Foreign Keys\n43\t**Estimate:** 0.25h\n44\t\n45\t**What:**\n46\t- In `db_session` fixture, after creating engine, execute:\n47\t  ```python\n48\t  from sqlalchemy import event\n49\t  @event.listens_for(test_engine, \"connect\")\n50\t  def set_sqlite_pragma(dbapi_conn, connection_record):\n51\t      cursor = dbapi_conn.cursor()\n52\t      cursor.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON\")\n53\t      cursor.close()\n54\t  ```\n55\t\n56\t**Why:**\n57\t- SQLite disables foreign key constraints by default\n58\t- Tests need FK enforcement (same as PostgreSQL)\n59\t\n60\t**How to validate:**\n61\t```python\n62\t# Test that FK violation raises error\n63\tdef test_fk_enforcement(db_session):\n64\t    from quantagent.models import Trade\n65\t    with pytest.raises(Exception):\n66\t        trade = Trade(order_id=99999)  # Non-existent order\n67\t        db_session.add(trade)\n68\t        db_session.commit()\n69\t```\n70\t\n71\t**Dependencies:** Task 1\n72\t\n73\t---\n74\t\n75\t### Task 3: Remove or Update Existing db_session Fixtures\n76\t**Estimate:** 0.25h\n77\t\n78\t**What:**\n79\t- Search for existing `db_session` fixtures in test files:\n80\t  ```bash\n81\t  grep -r \"def db_session\" tests/\n82\t  ```\n83\t- If found in `test_backtest.py` or other files, remove them (use centralized fixture from `conftest.py`)\n84\t- Update any test-specific cleanup logic if needed\n85\t\n86\t**Why:**\n87\t- Avoid fixture conflicts\n88\t- Single source of truth for test database setup\n89\t\n90\t**How to validate:**\n91\t```bash\n92\tpytest tests/ -v\n93\t# All tests using db_session pass\n94\t```\n95\t\n96\t**Dependencies:** Task 1\n97\t\n98\t---\n99\t\n100\t### Task 4: Run Full Test Suite\n101\t**Estimate:** 0.25h\n102\t\n103\t**What:**\n104\t- Execute full test suite:\n105\t  ```bash\n106\t  pytest tests/ -v\n107\t  ```\n108\t- Verify all unit tests pass\n109\t- Check for any tests failing due to SQLite incompatibilities\n110\t- Fix any issues (e.g., PostgreSQL-specific SQL)\n111\t\n112\t**Why:**\n113\t- Comprehensive validation\n114\t- Catch edge cases\n115\t\n116\t**How to validate:**\n117\t```bash\n118\tpytest tests/ -v | grep -E \"(PASSED|FAILED|ERROR)\" | sort | uniq -c\n119\t# Should show all PASSED, no FAILED/ERROR related to database\n120\t```\n121\t\n122\t**Dependencies:** Tasks 1-3\n123\t\n124\t---\n125\t\n126\t### Task 5: Document Changes (Optional)\n127\t**Estimate:** 0.25h\n128\t\n129\t**What:**\n130\t- Update `docs/03_design/TESTING_PATTERNS.md` with database testing guidance:\n131\t  - How to use `db_session` fixture\n132\t  - SQLite vs PostgreSQL considerations\n133\t  - When to use integration tests for PostgreSQL-specific features\n134\t\n135\t**Why:**\n136\t- Help future developers understand test database setup\n137\t- Prevent regressions\n138\t\n139\t**How to validate:**\n140\t- Read doc and verify clarity\n141\t- Ensure examples are accurate\n142\t\n143\t**Dependencies:** Task 4\n144\t\n145\t---\n146\t\n147\t## Total Estimate\n148\t\n149\t**1.5 hours** (3 core tasks + 2 optional/validation tasks)\n150\t\n151\t---\n152\t\n153\t## Execution Order\n154\t\n155\t1. **Task 1** (core fix)\n156\t2. **Task 2** (FK enforcement)\n157\t3. **Task 3** (cleanup)\n158\t4. **Task 4** (validation)\n159\t5. **Task 5** (documentation) — optional, can be deferred\n160\t\n161\t---\n162\t\n163\t## Risks & Mitigations\n164\t\n165\t### Risk 1: SQLite Incompatibility\n166\t**Description:** Some tests may use PostgreSQL-specific features (ENUM, ARRAY, etc.)\n167\t\n168\t**Mitigation:**\n169\t- QuantAgent models use standard SQLAlchemy types (no PostgreSQL-specific types identified)\n170\t- If issues arise, wrap PostgreSQL-specific tests with `@pytest.mark.postgres` and skip in unit tests\n171\t\n172\t**Probability:** Low  \n173\t**Impact:** Low\n174\t\n175\t---\n176\t\n177\t### Risk 2: Test Cleanup Incomplete\n178\t**Description:** Fixture cleanup may leave state (if using file-based SQLite)\n179\t\n180\t**Mitigation:**\n181\t- Use in-memory SQLite (`:memory:`) — automatically cleaned up on session close\n182\t- Explicitly drop tables and dispose engine in fixture cleanup\n183\t\n184\t**Probability:** Very Low  \n185\t**Impact:** Low\n186\t\n187\t---\n188\t\n189\t### Risk 3: Foreign Key Constraint Differences\n190\t**Description:** SQLite FK enforcement may differ from PostgreSQL\n191\t\n192\t**Mitigation:**\n193\t- Explicitly enable FK constraints in SQLite (`PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON`)\n194\t- Task 2 addresses this\n195\t\n196\t**Probability:** Low (with mitigation)  \n197\t**Impact:** Medium\n198\t\n199\t---\n200\t\n201\t## Testing Strategy\n202\t\n203\t### Unit Tests (SQLite)\n204\t- All tests using `db_session` fixture\n205\t- Fast, isolated, no external dependencies\n206\t- Run on every commit\n207\t\n208\t### Integration Tests (PostgreSQL) — Future\n209\t- If PostgreSQL-specific features are tested, mark with `@pytest.mark.integration`\n210\t- Skip by default (`pytest -m \"not integration\"`)\n211\t- Run manually or in CI with PostgreSQL service\n212\t\n213\t---\n214\t\n215\t## Rollout Plan\n216\t\n217\t### Step 1: Local Development\n218\t- Developer implements Tasks 1-3\n219\t- Runs `pytest tests/` locally\n220\t- Verifies all tests pass\n221\t\n222\t### Step 2: Code Review\n223\t- Submit PR with:\n224\t  - Updated `tests/conftest.py`\n225\t  - This planning doc + RQ/DS/AC docs\n226\t- Reviewer runs tests locally\n227\t\n228\t### Step 3: CI Validation\n229\t- CI pipeline runs `pytest tests/`\n230\t- Verifies tests pass in clean environment (no PostgreSQL)\n231\t\n232\t### Step 4: Merge to Main\n233\t- Once approved and CI passes, merge\n234\t- All future tests benefit from SQLite fixture\n235\t\n236\t---\n237\t\n238\t## Success Criteria\n239\t\n240\t- [ ] All unit tests pass with `pytest tests/`\n241\t- [ ] No `psycopg2.OperationalError` errors\n242\t- [ ] Tests run in < 60s (target: < 30s)\n243\t- [ ] No PostgreSQL required for unit tests\n244\t- [ ] Documentation updated (optional)\n245\t\n246\t---\n247\t\n248\t## Next Steps After This Issue\n249\t\n250\t1. **Implementer Agent**: Execute Tasks 1-4\n251\t2. **Tester Agent**: Run test suite, verify all ACs\n252\t3. **Merge**: Squash commit to main branch\n253\t4. **Close Issue**: Update Beads status to `closed`\n254\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c1eaaa5-4630-4080-9c30-fa243b2053bf","uuid":"f6244493-2173-40b3-a346-be6410c8dfbb","timestamp":"2026-05-08T02:42:56.301Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/azureuser/repos/projects/QuantAgent/docs/02_planning/QuantAgent-4ch-PL-test-db-configuration.md","content":"# QuantAgent-4ch — Planning: Test Database Configuration\n\n**Issue ID:** QuantAgent-4ch  \n**Title:** Fix remaining unit test failures (stale paths and missing data)  \n**Type:** Bug  \n**Priority:** 1\n\n---\n\n## Objective\n\nFix unit test failures by replacing PostgreSQL database dependency with SQLite for tests.\n\n---\n\n## Tasks\n\n### Task 1: Update conftest.py with db_session Fixture\n**Estimate:** 0.5h\n\n**What:**\n- Add `db_session` fixture to `tests/conftest.py`\n- Use SQLite in-memory engine (`sqlite:///:memory:`)\n- Create all tables via `Base.metadata.create_all()`\n- Yield session for test use\n- Cleanup: close session, drop tables, dispose engine\n\n**Why:**\n- Provides isolated, fast test database\n- No external dependencies (PostgreSQL)\n\n**How to validate:**\n```bash\npytest tests/test_backtest.py::TestBacktest::test_backtest_initialization -v\n# Should PASS (no psycopg2 errors)\n```\n\n**Dependencies:** None\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Enable SQLite Foreign Keys\n**Estimate:** 0.25h\n\n**What:**\n- In `db_session` fixture, after creating engine, execute:\n  ```python\n  from sqlalchemy import event\n  @event.listens_for(test_engine, \"connect\")\n  def set_sqlite_pragma(dbapi_conn, connection_record):\n      cursor = dbapi_conn.cursor()\n      cursor.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON\")\n      cursor.close()\n  ```\n\n**Why:**\n- SQLite disables foreign key constraints by default\n- Tests need FK enforcement (same as PostgreSQL)\n\n**How to validate:**\n```python\n# Test that FK violation raises error\ndef test_fk_enforcement(db_session):\n    from quantagent.models import Trade\n    with pytest.raises(Exception):\n        trade = Trade(order_id=99999)  # Non-existent order\n        db_session.add(trade)\n        db_session.commit()\n```\n\n**Dependencies:** Task 1\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Remove or Update Existing db_session Fixtures\n**Estimate:** 0.25h\n\n**What:**\n- Search for existing `db_session` fixtures in test files:\n  ```bash\n  grep -r \"def db_session\" tests/\n  ```\n- If found in `test_backtest.py` or other files, remove them (use centralized fixture from `conftest.py`)\n- Update any test-specific cleanup logic if needed\n\n**Why:**\n- Avoid fixture conflicts\n- Single source of truth for test database setup\n\n**How to validate:**\n```bash\npytest tests/ -v\n# All tests using db_session pass\n```\n\n**Dependencies:** Task 1\n\n---\n\n### Task 4: Run Full Test Suite\n**Estimate:** 0.25h\n\n**What:**\n- Execute full test suite:\n  ```bash\n  pytest tests/ -v\n  ```\n- Verify all unit tests pass\n- Check for any tests failing due to SQLite incompatibilities\n- Fix any issues (e.g., PostgreSQL-specific SQL)\n\n**Why:**\n- Comprehensive validation\n- Catch edge cases\n\n**How to validate:**\n```bash\npytest tests/ -v | grep -E \"(PASSED|FAILED|ERROR)\" | sort | uniq -c\n# Should show all PASSED, no FAILED/ERROR related to database\n```\n\n**Dependencies:** Tasks 1-3\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: Document Changes (Optional)\n**Estimate:** 0.25h\n\n**What:**\n- Update `docs/03_design/TESTING_PATTERNS.md` with database testing guidance:\n  - How to use `db_session` fixture\n  - SQLite vs PostgreSQL considerations\n  - When to use integration tests for PostgreSQL-specific features\n\n**Why:**\n- Help future developers understand test database setup\n- Prevent regressions\n\n**How to validate:**\n- Read doc and verify clarity\n- Ensure examples are accurate\n\n**Dependencies:** Task 4\n\n---\n\n## Total Estimate\n\n**1.5 hours** (3 core tasks + 2 optional/validation tasks)\n\n---\n\n## Execution Order\n\n1. **Task 1** (core fix)\n2. **Task 2** (FK enforcement)\n3. **Task 3** (cleanup)\n4. **Task 4** (validation)\n5. **Task 5** (documentation) — optional, can be deferred\n\n---\n\n## Risks & Mitigations\n\n### Risk 1: SQLite Incompatibility\n**Description:** Some tests may use PostgreSQL-specific features (ENUM, ARRAY, etc.)\n\n**Mitigation:**\n- QuantAgent models use standard SQLAlchemy types (no PostgreSQL-specific types identified)\n- If issues arise, wrap PostgreSQL-specific tests with `@pytest.mark.postgres` and skip in unit tests\n\n**Probability:** Low  \n**Impact:** Low\n\n---\n\n### Risk 2: Test Cleanup Incomplete\n**Description:** Fixture cleanup may leave state (if using file-based SQLite)\n\n**Mitigation:**\n- Use in-memory SQLite (`:memory:`) — automatically cleaned up on session close\n- Explicitly drop tables and dispose engine in fixture cleanup\n\n**Probability:** Very Low  \n**Impact:** Low\n\n---\n\n### Risk 3: Foreign Key Constraint Differences\n**Description:** SQLite FK enforcement may differ from PostgreSQL\n\n**Mitigation:**\n- Explicitly enable FK constraints in SQLite (`PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON`)\n- Task 2 addresses this\n\n**Probability:** Low (with mitigation)  \n**Impact:** Medium\n\n---\n\n## Testing Strategy\n\n### Unit Tests (SQLite)\n- All tests using `db_session` fixture\n- Fast, isolated, no external dependencies\n- Run on every commit\n\n### Integration Tests (PostgreSQL) — Future\n- If PostgreSQL-specific features are tested, mark with `@pytest.mark.integration`\n- Skip by default (`pytest -m \"not integration\"`)\n- Run manually or in CI with PostgreSQL service\n\n---\n\n## Rollout Plan\n\n### Step 1: Local Development\n- Developer implements Tasks 1-3\n- Runs `pytest tests/` locally\n- Verifies all tests pass\n\n### Step 2: Code Review\n- Submit PR with:\n  - Updated `tests/conftest.py`\n  - This planning doc + RQ/DS/AC docs\n- Reviewer runs tests locally\n\n### Step 3: CI Validation\n- CI pipeline runs `pytest tests/`\n- Verifies tests pass in clean environment (no PostgreSQL)\n\n### Step 4: Merge to Main\n- Once approved and CI passes, merge\n- All future tests benefit from SQLite fixture\n\n---\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [ ] All unit tests pass with `pytest tests/`\n- [ ] No `psycopg2.OperationalError` errors\n- [ ] Tests run in < 60s (target: < 30s)\n- [ ] No PostgreSQL required for unit tests\n- [ ] Documentation updated (optional)\n\n---\n\n## Next Steps After This Issue\n\n1. **Implementer Agent**: Execute Tasks 1-4\n2. **Tester Agent**: Run test suite, verify all ACs\n3. **Merge**: Squash commit to main branch\n4. **Close Issue**: Update Beads status to `closed`\n","numLines":254,"startLine":1,"totalLines":254}}}
